 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Input",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Runs from AC between 90 and 305 VAC at 47 to 440 Hz, or from DC between 100 and 430 VDC with either input polarity. Certified ranges are 100 - 250 VDC and 50/60 Hz; the AC rated range is 100 - 277 VAC under 62368-1 and 100 - 240 VAC, AC only, under 60335-1. A 1'600 mA slow-blow fuse is the recommended input protection."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Load",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "No minimum load is needed. Each model has its own ceiling on output capacitance: 3'500 µF at 3.3 V, 2'500 µF at 5 V, 470 µF at 12 V and 150 µF at 24 V. Ripple figures are taken with 0.1 µF and 47 µF in parallel across the output, measured in a 20 MHz bandwidth."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Protection",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "A short on the output can be held indefinitely; the module recovers by itself once it is removed. Output current is limited somewhere between 115 % and 195 % of the rated maximum. A Zener diode clamps the output between 105 % and 145 % of nominal voltage on overvoltage."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Start-up and hold-up",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The output comes up within 60 ms at either 115 or 230 VAC, and stays up for at least 15 ms after the 230 VAC input is lost."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Derating and cooling",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Cooling is by natural convection (20 LFM). Output power is derated by 2.5 % per kelvin above 50 °C and by 2.0 % per kelvin below -30 °C, within the -40 °C to +70 °C operating range."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Isolation and safety",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Input and output are separated by reinforced insulation, rated for a working voltage of 314 VAC and tested at 4'000 VAC for 60 s; touch current is at most 250 µA. The module is prepared for protection class I and II equipment. Under 62368-1 its output is classed ES1 and PS3. It is rated for pollution degree 2 and overvoltage category II, and for altitudes up to 5'000 m (62368-1) or 2'000 m (60335-1)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Assembly",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Through-hole module for lead-free wave soldering at no more than 270 °C for 3 s. Washing is not allowed."
  }
 ],
